/-!
# The dimension of a projective linear subspace

A submodule `W` of a vector space `V` cuts out the projective linear subspace
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpaceOfModule.linearSubspace k V W` of `𝐏(V) = Proj (Sym_k V)`, the
projective zero locus of the degree-one forms coming from `W`. The *quotient* map `V ⟶ V ⧸ W`
induces a surjection of symmetric algebras whose kernel is exactly the ideal cutting out `L(W)`,
so `L(W)` is the projective space of `V ⧸ W` and has dimension `dim_k (V ⧸ W) - 1`. For `W` of
corank two — the forms vanishing at two distinct closed points — that dimension is one: the line
joining them really is a line.

## Main results

* `SymPow.symAlgMap_surjective`: `Sym` of a surjective linear map is surjective.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpaceOfModule.linearSubspace_eq_zeroLocus_ker`: the equations of
  `L(W)` are the kernel of `Sym_k V ⟶ Sym_k (V ⧸ W)`, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpaceOfModule.linearSubspaceHomeomorph`: **`L(W)` is
  homeomorphic to `𝐏(V ⧸ W)`.**
* `ProjectiveSpaceOfModule.topologicalKrullDim_linearSubspace_of_finrank_quotient_eq` and
  `ProjectiveSpaceOfModule.topologicalKrullDim_linearSubspace_add_one` (in `AlgebraicGeometry`):
  **the dimension of a projective linear subspace**, as `dim L(W) = n` from
  `dim_k (V ⧸ W) = n + 1` and in the subtraction-free form `dim L(W) + 1 = dim_k (V ⧸ W)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpaceOfModule.topologicalKrullDim_linearSubspace_eq_zero` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpaceOfModule.topologicalKrullDim_linearSubspace_lineSubmodule`:
  a submodule of corank one cuts out a point and one of corank two a curve of dimension one, so
  **the line through two distinct closed points has dimension one.**

## Implementation notes

The dimension of `L(W)` is reached through the *topology* of the projective spectra and not
through the closed immersion of schemes `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` is: the general statement
is `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.homeomorphZeroLocusKer`, that `Proj ℬ` is homeomorphic
to the zero locus of the kernel for a surjective graded homomorphism, and Krull dimension is a
homeomorphism invariant. Everything scheme-theoretic about `Proj.map` would have to be unwound
again to say the same thing about underlying spaces. The dimension of `𝐏(V ⧸ W)` itself is
`AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDim_projectiveSpaceOfModule_add_one`, so this file is in a
single universe, as that statement requires.

The two-sided identification `linearSubspace k V W = zeroLocus (ker ...)` is applied through
`Homeomorph.setCongr` rather than by rewriting under `topologicalKrullDim`: the ambient type of
the left side is the carrier of the scheme `projectiveSpaceOfModule k V` and of the right side
the bare `ProjectiveSpectrum`, and although the two are definitionally equal, `rw` type-checks
its motive at a transparency at which they are not.

These statements are separated from
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Variety.Projective.LinesAvoidingSubvariety`, where the subspace
itself is constructed, because `topologicalKrullDim_projectiveSpaceOfModule_of_finrank_eq` brings
most of the library into the import closure. Carrying that into the file defining
`linearSubspace` would carry it into everything using a linear subspace, where the instances it
adds overrun the instance-search budget of unrelated typeclass goals.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B2T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B2T)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B1R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B1R)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace

namespace SymPow

/-- **`Sym` of a surjective linear map is surjective.** The symmetric algebra is generated by its
degree-one part together with the scalars, and every degree-one generator of the target is the
image of one of the source. -/
public theorem symAlgMap_surjective {R M N : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] (f : M →ₗ[R] N) (hf : Function.Surjective f) :
    Function.Surjective (symAlgMap f) := by
  intro z
  induction z using SymmetricAlgebra.induction with
  | algebraMap r => exact ⟨algebraMap R _ r, AlgHom.commutes _ r⟩
  | ι x =>
    obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := hf x
    exact ⟨SymmetricAlgebra.ι R M m, symAlgMap_ι f m⟩
  | mul a b ha hb =>
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := ha
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hb
    exact ⟨x * y, map_mul _ _ _⟩
  | add a b ha hb =>
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := ha
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hb
    exact ⟨x + y, map_add _ _ _⟩

end SymPow

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpaceOfModule

universe u

variable {k V : Type u} [Field k] [AddCommGroup V] [Module k V]

/-- The graded homomorphism of symmetric algebras induced by the quotient map by `W` is
surjective. -/
@[ega "II 4.1.2" "special case"]
public theorem surjective_gradedSymAlgMap_mkQ (W : Submodule k V) :
    Function.Surjective (SymPow.gradedSymAlgMap W.mkQ) :=
  SymPow.symAlgMap_surjective W.mkQ W.mkQ_surjective

/-- The quotient map by `W` meets Mathlib's side condition for `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map`: the
irrelevant ideal of `Sym_k (V ⧸ W)` lies in the image of that of `Sym_k V`. -/
public theorem irrelevant_le_map_gradedSymAlgMap_mkQ (W : Submodule k V) :
    HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (fun n => SymPow.symmetricPower n k (V ⧸ W)) ≤
      (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (fun n => SymPow.symmetricPower n k V)).map
        (SymPow.gradedSymAlgMap W.mkQ) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.irrelevant_le_map_of_surjective _ (surjective_gradedSymAlgMap_mkQ W)

/-- **The equations of a projective linear subspace are the kernel of `Sym` of the quotient
map.** The kernel of `Sym_k V ⟶ Sym_k (V ⧸ W)` is the ideal generated by `ι W`, which is the set
of degree-one equations cutting out `linearSubspace k V W`. -/
public theorem linearSubspace_eq_zeroLocus_ker (W : Submodule k V) :
    linearSubspace k V W = ProjectiveSpectrum.zeroLocus
      (fun n => SymPow.symmetricPower n k V)
      (RingHom.ker (SymPow.gradedSymAlgMap W.mkQ)) := by
  have hker : RingHom.ker (SymPow.gradedSymAlgMap W.mkQ) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range ((SymmetricAlgebra.ι k V) ∘ ((↑) : W → V))) := by
    have h := Stacks.Chow.GenuineChern.ker_symAlgMap_eq_span W.mkQ W.mkQ_surjective
    rw [Submodule.ker_mkQ] at h
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (h.trans ?_)
    · exact Ideal.ext fun z => Iff.rfl
    · congr 1
      ext y
      simp
  rw [linearSubspace, hker, ProjectiveSpectrum.zeroLocus_span]

/-- **A projective linear subspace is the projective space of the quotient.** The subspace of
`𝐏(V)` cut out by `W` is homeomorphic to `𝐏(V ⧸ W)`, by `Proj` of the surjection
`Sym_k V ⟶ Sym_k (V ⧸ W)`. -/
public noncomputable def linearSubspaceHomeomorph (W : Submodule k V) :
    projectiveSpaceOfModule k (V ⧸ W) ≃ₜ linearSubspace k V W :=
  (ProjectiveSpectrum.homeomorphZeroLocusKer (SymPow.gradedSymAlgMap W.mkQ)
      (irrelevant_le_map_gradedSymAlgMap_mkQ W) (surjective_gradedSymAlgMap_mkQ W)).trans
    (Homeomorph.setCongr (linearSubspace_eq_zeroLocus_ker W).symm)

/-- **The dimension of a projective linear subspace.** The subspace of `𝐏(V)` cut out by a
submodule `W` whose quotient has dimension `n + 1` has Krull dimension `n`: it is `𝐏(V ⧸ W)`. -/
public theorem topologicalKrullDim_linearSubspace_of_finrank_quotient_eq [FiniteDimensional k V]
    {W : Submodule k V} {n : ℕ} (hW : Module.finrank k (V ⧸ W) = n + 1) :
    topologicalKrullDim (linearSubspace k V W) = (n : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
  (IsHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq _
    (linearSubspaceHomeomorph W).symm.isHomeomorph).trans
      (topologicalKrullDim_projectiveSpaceOfModule_of_finrank_eq hW)

/-- **The dimension of a projective linear subspace**, stated without subtraction: for a proper
submodule `W` of a finite-dimensional `V`,
`dim L(W) + 1 = dim_k (V ⧸ W)`. -/
public theorem topologicalKrullDim_linearSubspace_add_one [FiniteDimensional k V]
    {W : Submodule k V} (hW : W ≠ ⊤) :
    topologicalKrullDim (linearSubspace k V W) + 1 =
      (Module.finrank k (V ⧸ W) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have hnt : Nontrivial (V ⧸ W) := Submodule.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hW
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ : ∃ n, Module.finrank k (V ⧸ W) = n + 1 :=
    ⟨Module.finrank k (V ⧸ W) - 1, by
      have := Module.finrank_pos (R := k) (M := V ⧸ W); omega⟩
  rw [topologicalKrullDim_linearSubspace_of_finrank_quotient_eq hn, hn]
  push_cast
  rfl

/-- **The subspace cut out by a submodule of corank one is a point**, dimension zero. -/
public theorem topologicalKrullDim_linearSubspace_eq_zero [FiniteDimensional k V]
    {W : Submodule k V} (hW : Module.finrank k (V ⧸ W) = 1) :
    topologicalKrullDim (linearSubspace k V W) = 0 :=
  topologicalKrullDim_linearSubspace_of_finrank_quotient_eq (n := 0) (by simpa using hW)

/-- **The line through two distinct closed points of `𝐏(V)` has dimension one.** The degree-one
forms vanishing at both have corank two, so the linear subspace they cut out is a projective
line. -/
public theorem topologicalKrullDim_linearSubspace_lineSubmodule [IsAlgClosed k]
    [FiniteDimensional k V] {p q : projectiveSpaceOfModule k V}
    (hp : IsClosed ({p} : Set (projectiveSpaceOfModule k V)))
    (hq : IsClosed ({q} : Set (projectiveSpaceOfModule k V))) (hpq : p ≠ q) :
    topologicalKrullDim (linearSubspace k V (lineSubmodule k V p q)) = 1 :=
  topologicalKrullDim_linearSubspace_of_finrank_quotient_eq (n := 1)
    (by simpa using finrank_quotient_lineSubmodule k V hp hq hpq)

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpaceOfModule

end
